    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366">

                <pb facs="0410" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg312"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States.</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-12"><hi rendition="#italic">July 12,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 690.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In presenting to Mr. Delcassé your cables
                    defining our attitude in China I found that he considered the situation about as
                    we did. He expressed himself in like manner in the Chamber of Deputies, and <pb
                        facs="0411" n="313" xml:id="pg313"/> I send you herewith a translation of
                    statements he made in that body on the 3d and 8th instant, by which you will see
                    that his definition of the policy of France in China substantially agrees with
                    us.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Horace Porter.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d366-a1.xml" xpointer="d366-a1"/>
            </div>
